# Avatar Standard: Use UserAvatar Component

All user avatars in CentaurOS **must** use the standardized `UserAvatar` component to ensure consistent role-based color coding across the application.

## Required Import

```tsx
import { UserAvatar, UserAvatarStack } from "@/components/ui/user-avatar"
```

## DO NOT use raw Avatar components for users

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - Do not do this
import { Avatar, AvatarFallback } from "@/components/ui/avatar"
<Avatar>
  <AvatarFallback className="bg-slate-100">JD</AvatarFallback>
</Avatar>

// ✅ CORRECT - Use UserAvatar instead
import { UserAvatar } from "@/components/ui/user-avatar"
<UserAvatar name="John Doe" role="Executive" size="md" />
```

## Role-Based Color System

The `UserAvatar` component automatically applies colors based on user role using an **orange hierarchy** for leadership:

| Role | Background | Text | Use Case |
|------|------------|------|----------|
| `Founder` | `bg-orange-100` | `text-orange-700` | Company founders (dark orange) |
| `Executive` | `bg-orange-50` | `text-orange-600` | Executive team members (light orange) |
| `Apprentice` | `bg-muted` | `text-muted-foreground` | Apprentices/interns (neutral) |
| `AI_Agent` | `bg-purple-100` | `text-purple-600` | AI assistants (purple) |
| Default | `bg-muted` | `text-muted-foreground` | Any other role (neutral) |

**Visual Hierarchy:** The orange tones create a clear visual hierarchy - Founders stand out with darker orange, Executives with lighter orange, while Apprentices use neutral tones to not compete for attention.

## Component Props

```tsx
interface UserAvatarProps {
  name: string | null | undefined    // User's full name for initials
  role?: string | null               // Role for color coding
  avatarUrl?: string | null          // Optional profile image
  size?: "xs" | "sm" | "md" | "lg" | "xl"  // Size variant
  className?: string                 // Additional classes
}
```

**IMPORTANT:** Avatars must be clean circles without borders or rings. The bordered avatar style has been removed from the design system.

## Size Reference

| Size | Dimensions | Text Size | Use Case |
|------|------------|-----------|----------|
| `xs` | `h-4 w-4` | `text-[6px]` | Inline mentions, tiny indicators |
| `sm` | `h-6 w-6` | `text-[10px]` | Compact lists, dropdowns |
| `md` | `h-8 w-8` | `text-xs` | Default, cards, messages |
| `lg` | `h-10 w-10` | `text-sm` | Profile headers, prominent display |
| `xl` | `h-14 w-14` | `text-xl` | Large profile cards |
| `2xl` | `h-20 w-20` | `text-2xl` | Public profile views |
| `3xl` | `h-24 w-24` | `text-3xl` | Full profile pages |

## CRITICAL Anti-Patterns (NEVER Do This)

During avatar standardization, we found **35+ inconsistent implementations** across 23 files. These are the exact violations found and how to fix them.

### ❌ Anti-Pattern #1: Custom Avatar Components

**Found in:** 2 files (GanttView.tsx, TimelineListView.tsx)

**The Problem:** Creating custom avatar components that duplicate `UserAvatar` functionality.

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - Custom InitialsAvatar component
const InitialsAvatar = ({ name, color }: { name: string; color: string }) => {
  const getInitials = (name: string) => {
    return name.split(' ').map(n => n[0]).join('').slice(0, 2)
  }
  
  return (
    <div className={`h-8 w-8 rounded-full bg-${color}-100 text-${color}-700`}>
      {getInitials(name)}
    </div>
  )
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Use UserAvatar
import { UserAvatar } from '@/components/ui/user-avatar'
<UserAvatar name="John Doe" role="Executive" size="md" />
```

---

### ❌ Anti-Pattern #2: Direct Avatar with Hardcoded `bg-muted`

**Found in:** 8 files

**The Problem:** Using `Avatar` directly with hardcoded gray background instead of role-based colors.

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - Hardcoded bg-muted
import { Avatar, AvatarFallback, AvatarImage } from '@/components/ui/avatar'

<Avatar>
  <AvatarFallback className="bg-muted text-muted-foreground">
    {getInitials(user.full_name)}
  </AvatarFallback>
</Avatar>

// ✅ CORRECT - UserAvatar with role-based colors
import { UserAvatar } from '@/components/ui/user-avatar'
<UserAvatar name={user.full_name} role={user.role} size="md" />
```

---

### ❌ Anti-Pattern #3: Hardcoded `bg-foundry-*` Colors

**Found in:** task-feed.tsx

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG
<AvatarFallback className="bg-foundry-700 text-white">
  {task.user?.full_name?.split(' ').map(n => n[0]).join('')}
</AvatarFallback>

// ✅ CORRECT
<UserAvatar name={task.user?.full_name} role={task.user?.role} size="md" />
```

